 {
  "ms": 7151,
  "type": "agent_response",
  "text": "The sky went pink first, then orange, spilling over the ridge like someone had cracked the world open. The peaks caught the light before anything else — sharp and dark against all that color, like they were holding it up. Down in the valley, everything was still blue and quiet, waiting its turn. And then the sun cleared the ridge properly, and suddenly the whole mountainside was gold, and the cold air didn't feel as heavy anymore.",
  "event_id": 1
 },
